    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section describes the Body Image Screening Questionnaire for Eating Disorder Early Detection (BISQ), a 24-item, 6-point scale measuring five dimensions of disordered eating; the authors used an overall BISQ score (mean of items) due to inadequate internal consistency for most subscales. It reports that in prior Romanian translation work total scores had Cronbach's alpha = .85 and that in the present study the overall BISQ Cronbach's alpha was .82 for women and .80 for men. No information about sample size, demographics, country, BMI assessment, body appreciation measures, survey method, or number of studies is provided in this section.",
      "evidence_source": "\"This is a 24-item scale that measures symptomatology of disordered eating along five dimensions... Items were rated on a 6-point scale (1 = Never, 6 = Always).\"; \"However, total scores were reported to yield evidence of internal consistency (Cronbach \u02db= .85) and discriminant validity.\"; \"Cronbach's alpha for the overall score in the present study was .82 for women and .80 for men.\"",
